{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2020-01-19T14:09:55.230872+00:00", "modified": "2021-08-12T08:11:38.485970+00:00", "id": 3612479, "conceptrecid": "3588515", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3588515", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "metadata": {"title": "Predicting the Costs of Serverless Workflows - Replication package", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "publication_date": "2019-12-20", "description": "<p>Function-as-a-Service (FaaS) platforms enable users to run arbitrary functions without being concerned about operational issues, while only paying for the consumed resources. Individual functions are often composed into workflows for complex tasks. However, the pay-per-use model and nontransparent reporting by cloud providers make it challenging to estimate the expected cost of a workflow, which prevents informed business decisions. In our paper, we propose a methodology for the cost prediction of serverless workflows consisting of input-parameter sensitive function models and a monte-carlo simulation of an abstract workflow model.</p>\n\n<p>Reproducing the results from this paper consists of two parts reproducing the performance measurements for the audio processing functions in the Google Functions environment and reproducing the performance predictions using the proposed approach based on the collected measurement data. In order to enable quick reproduction of the performance measurements, we packaged the scripts for the experiment automation as a docker container. The original measurement data used in the paper and the python code implementing the proposed approach are available in form of a CodeOcean capsule, which enables quick and easy reproduction of our results.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Simon Eismann", "affiliation": "University of W\u00fcrzburg"}, {"name": "Johannes Grohmann", "affiliation": "University of W\u00fcrzburg"}, {"name": "Erwin van Eyk", "affiliation": "Delft University of Technology"}, {"name": "Nikolas Herbst", "affiliation": "University of W\u00fcrzburg"}, {"name": "Samuel Kounev", "affiliation": "University of W\u00fcrzburg"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "3588515"}}]}}, "title": "Predicting the Costs of Serverless Workflows - Replication package", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3612479", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3612479?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.3612479", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3588515", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3588515", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3588515", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.3588515", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:3612479/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:3612479/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3612479/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/requests"}, "updated": "2021-08-12T08:11:38.485970+00:00", "recid": "3612479", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "0edac79b-f40b-4a43-8596-7278d6ac1d91", "key": "ICPE2020_Cost_Prediction_of_Serverless_Workflows.rar", "size": 28107403, "checksum": "md5:b933c36f4dc7408b2c49f836532cdd4a", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3612479/files/ICPE2020_Cost_Prediction_of_Serverless_Workflows.rar/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "47852"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 110, "unique_downloads": 110, "views": 260, "unique_views": 246, "version_downloads": 40, "version_unique_downloads": 40, "version_unique_views": 128, "version_views": 134}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2019-10-08T19:33:01.975679+00:00", "modified": "2020-01-25T07:23:47.384411+00:00", "id": 3477414, "conceptrecid": "3477413", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3477414", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3477413", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3477414", "metadata": {"title": "Replication Package \"Testing with Fewer Resources: An Adaptive Approach to Performance-Aware Test Case Generation\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3477414", "publication_date": "2019-10-08", "description": "<p>Automated test case generation is an effective technique to yield high-coverage test suites.&nbsp;While the majority of research effort has been devoted to satisfying coverage criteria, a recent trend emerged towards optimizing other non-coverage aspects. In this regard, runtime and memory usage are two essential dimensions: less expensive tests reduce the resource demands for the generation process and later regression testing phases.<br>\nThis study shows that performance-aware&nbsp;test case generation requires solving two main challenges: providing a good approximation of resource usage with minimal overhead and avoiding detrimental effects on both final coverage and fault detection effectiveness.&nbsp;To tackle these challenges, we conceived a set of performance proxies ---inspired by previous work on performance testing--- that provide a reasonable estimation of the test execution costs (i.e., runtime and memory usage).<br>\nThus, we propose an adaptive strategy, called aDynaMOSA, which leverages these proxies by extending DynaMOSA, a state-of-the-art evolutionary algorithm in unit testing.<br>\nOur empirical study ---involving 110 non-trivial Java classes--- reveals&nbsp;that our adaptive approach generates test suite with statistically significant improvements in runtime (-25%) and heap memory consumption (-15%) compared to DynaMOSA. Additionally, aDynaMOSA has comparable results to DynaMOSA over seven different coverage criteria and similar fault detection effectiveness.<br>\nOur empirical investigation also highlights that the usage of performance proxies (i.e., without the adaptiveness) is not sufficient to generate more performant test cases without compromising the overall coverage.&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Giovanni Grano", "affiliation": "University of Zurich", "orcid": "0000-0002-8207-3259"}, {"name": "Christoph Laaber", "affiliation": "University of Zurich", "orcid": "0000-0001-6817-331X"}, {"name": "Annibale Panichella", "affiliation": "Delft University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-7395-3588"}, {"name": "Sebastiano Panichella", "affiliation": "Zurich University of Applied Science", "orcid": "0000-0003-4120-626X"}], "